1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,510
A supervisor has to staff a mission and see where the team is thin.

2
00:00:04,510 --> 00:00:09,289
Nobody wants a hidden skills score, and a résumé is a claim, not proof.

3
00:00:09,289 --> 00:00:13,462
Shellback shows only what people confirmed and chose to share.

4
00:00:13,462 --> 00:00:15,886
Everyone in this video is fictional.

5
00:00:16,446 --> 00:00:17,648
Here is how it works.

6
00:00:17,648 --> 00:00:26,378
It all runs on this one computer: a small PowerShell server on loopback serves the app, and the app runs in your browser.

7
00:00:27,078 --> 00:00:31,038
Your workspace is stored in the browser, and exports can be encrypted.

8
00:00:31,738 --> 00:00:36,525
A résumé goes in as pasted text, a text file, a Word file, or the text layer of a PDF.

9
00:00:36,525 --> 00:00:38,909
Peer cards and an HR feed come in as files.

10
00:00:39,609 --> 00:00:46,954
Out come suggestions you confirm, and team coverage from three or more people who opted in.

11
00:00:46,954 --> 00:00:49,313
All of it works offline, with no AI.

12
00:00:50,154 --> 00:00:51,028
AI is optional.

13
00:00:51,028 --> 00:00:55,701
The model key sits in Lazarette, shared to Fairlead.

14
00:00:55,701 --> 00:01:03,614
Shellback has its own Fairlead key, sealed in the browser with your passphrase, and it calls Fairlead directly.

15
00:01:04,177 --> 00:01:08,650
An opt-in peer card is a plain file Halyard can read for planning.

16
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:13,546
A live Halyard link, and a git or CI runner, are planned, not built.

17
00:01:14,125 --> 00:01:25,805
And the guardrails: loopback and a strict content policy, nothing shared without opt-in, three people before any aggregate, and you confirm every skill.

18
00:01:26,202 --> 00:01:29,993
The model key lives in Lazarette, the encrypted vault on this machine.

19
00:01:29,993 --> 00:01:36,177
This footage is from the Halyard demo: it is the same key, set up once for every tool.

20
00:01:36,578 --> 00:01:39,400
Test credential checks it against OpenAI's read-only endpoint.

21
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,323
HTTP two hundred, so the key is good.

22
00:01:42,801 --> 00:01:45,863
Then share it with Fairlead by name.

23
00:01:45,863 --> 00:01:47,659
Fairlead sees only what you share.

24
00:01:48,359 --> 00:01:51,847
Fairlead reads it from the vault and connects.

25
00:01:51,847 --> 00:01:55,470
Every model call Shellback makes goes through here.

26
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:59,793
Shellback gets its own Fairlead client key, so its calls can be told apart in the log.

27
00:02:00,493 --> 00:02:03,376
Fairlead keeps only a hash and shows the key once.

28
00:02:04,018 --> 00:02:05,862
Here is the Shellback client in the list.

29
00:02:06,562 --> 00:02:11,437
The page calls Fairlead directly, so Shellback's address is allowed as a browser origin.

30
00:02:12,137 --> 00:02:15,200
In Shellback, open Program, then Intelligence.

31
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:18,129
Choose the Fairlead router on this computer.

32
00:02:18,829 --> 00:02:20,790
By default it asks for local engines only.

33
00:02:21,656 --> 00:02:24,828
This demo machine has no local model, so I allow cloud engines.

34
00:02:25,634 --> 00:02:27,135
Only synthetic text goes through.

35
00:02:27,835 --> 00:02:28,825
Paste the client key.

36
00:02:28,825 --> 00:02:33,695
It is sealed with a passphrase in the browser and never stored in the clear.

37
00:02:34,395 --> 00:02:36,032
Test connection.

38
00:02:36,032 --> 00:02:40,617
Fairlead answers, ninety-two models are available, and Shellback is using GPT-5 mini.

39
00:02:41,367 --> 00:02:42,367
Meet the employee.

40
00:02:42,367 --> 00:02:46,395
Priya Natarajan is fictional, and so is her résumé.

41
00:02:46,395 --> 00:02:50,009
The file is read in the browser and nothing is stored.

42
00:02:50,709 --> 00:02:54,413
Find skill suggestions sends the text to a real model through Fairlead.

43
00:02:54,413 --> 00:02:57,395
This is the live wait, sped up.

44
00:02:58,095 --> 00:03:00,760
These are suggestions, not facts.

45
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:04,049
Priya confirms two and dismisses one.

46
00:03:04,049 --> 00:03:06,733
Nothing counts until she says so.

47
00:03:07,433 --> 00:03:09,267
Her confirmed skills form her web.

48
00:03:09,267 --> 00:03:14,628
Everything else stays a suggestion, and dismissed ones never come back.

49
00:03:15,231 --> 00:03:20,206
Now the supervisor's view: a synthetic team of twenty people who chose to share.

50
00:03:20,906 --> 00:03:24,543
Coverage by domain comes only from shared, confirmed skills.

51
00:03:24,543 --> 00:03:27,553
With fewer than three people, nothing shows.

52
00:03:28,253 --> 00:03:34,106
The supervisor brief shows exactly what it is built from: counts and skill names, never people.

53
00:03:34,806 --> 00:03:39,646
Write the brief, and those aggregate numbers go to the model through Fairlead.

54
00:03:39,646 --> 00:03:40,595
Live again, sped up.

55
00:03:41,295 --> 00:03:46,043
Plain language, no names, no scores, and it says it is aggregate.

56
00:03:46,743 --> 00:03:49,528
A mission needs AWS architecture from two people.

57
00:03:50,139 --> 00:03:53,433
Shellback checks that requirement against the people who opted in.

58
00:03:53,683 --> 00:03:57,258
Trust and data lists what leaves this computer.

59
00:03:57,258 --> 00:04:01,697
With the router selected it says so, and names what is never sent.

60
00:04:02,397 --> 00:04:04,515
Sharing is a choice, card by card.

61
00:04:05,215 --> 00:04:12,289
Export asks twice: how many skills will leave, and that the file cannot be recalled, then whether to encrypt it.

62
00:04:12,989 --> 00:04:14,817
The card holds confirmed skills only.

63
00:04:15,482 --> 00:04:17,569
This is the file Halyard planning reads today.

64
00:04:18,236 --> 00:04:19,245
A live link is planned.

65
00:04:19,945 --> 00:04:28,876
And the evidence trail for the AI is Fairlead's own request log: client Shellback, model GPT-5 mini, status two hundred.

66
00:04:28,876 --> 00:04:30,591
Claims stay claims.

67
00:04:30,591 --> 00:04:37,992
Everything here was synthetic, and a skill counts only when its owner confirms it.

68
00:04:37,992 --> 00:04:44,851
Not built yet: a live Halyard link, and the consent ledger in the interface.

69
00:04:44,851 --> 00:04:46,927
No scores, no rankings.
